243
00:30:45.608 --> 00:30:46.858
Throw this away.

244
00:30:49.691 --> 00:30:53.358
- Let me go!
- He insists on going out alone.

245
00:30:55.650 --> 00:30:58.066
- Grandma!
- I was just trying to help.

246
00:30:58.233 --> 00:31:01.733
Bonnie. I got him!
He's stealing my money!

247
00:31:01.900 --> 00:31:04.108
- Call the police!
- We just...

248
00:31:04.275 --> 00:31:06.608
- Grandma. how are you?
- Calm down.

249
00:31:06.775 --> 00:31:09.233
- Broken.
- Wait a minute. mom.

250
00:31:17.150 --> 00:31:21.025
- You thief!
- Oh my God...

251
00:31:26.608 --> 00:31:27.775
Dad?

252
00:31:33.525 --> 00:31:34.525
Dad.

253
00:31:39.608 --> 00:31:41.858
He's out of gas.

254
00:31:45.233 --> 00:31:48.066
- Don't worry about the garden.
- Someone has to do this.

255
00:31:48.858 --> 00:31:50.265
I will do it but...

256
00:31:50.277 --> 00:31:53.792
We gave you the house.
You left it in disrepair.

257
00:31:54.941 --> 00:31:56.858
Do you want to live in this dump?

258
00:32:23.983 --> 00:32:25.066
Dad...

259
00:32:27.400 --> 00:32:30.191
Dad. help me...

260
00:32:53.775 --> 00:32:55.191
We are inside.

261
00:33:01.733 --> 00:33:03.066
Let us in. dad.

262
00:33:05.316 --> 00:33:06.775
No problem.

263
00:33:07.983 --> 00:33:09.650
Don't fight.

264
00:33:11.775 --> 00:33:13.483
You can do.

265
00:33:14.066 --> 00:33:15.608
Continue.

266
00:33:16.108 --> 00:33:17.108
Do it!

267
00:33:22.441 --> 00:33:23.608
Edgar?

268
00:33:26.358 --> 00:33:28.191
Edgar. are you okay?

269
00:33:48.441 --> 00:33:51.441
Please don't say anything to my wife...

270
00:33:52.275 --> 00:33:54.275
I'll keep this. okay?

271
00:34:18.983 --> 00:34:20.150
- What happened?

272
00:34:21.816 --> 00:34:24.176
- I tripped in the basement. I
dropped the plates. I'm sorry.

273
00:34:24.200 --> 00:34:29.492
- Yes. I heard. eat this
Can you put it on your desk?

274
00:34:29.566 --> 00:34:31.358
Be careful. I did it myself.

275
00:34:33.525 --> 00:34:36.150
- Really?
- This is Niobe. the Greek queen.

276
00:34:36.316 --> 00:34:38.358
- Edgar's favorite.
- It's nice.

277
00:34:40.600 --> 00:34:44.517
- Why did you stop doing it?
- The children came first.

278
00:34:44.775 --> 00:34:47.783
Then my sister Bonnie got sick. And
my mother couldn't manage on her own.

279
00:34:50.150 --> 00:34:54.150
- “You were talented. what a shame.”
- "Why should it be a pity?"

280
00:34:55.058 --> 00:34:58.600
I was among the people I
loved and I built my life there.

281
00:35:01.141 --> 00:35:02.441
I am nothing without my family.

282
00:35:28.350 --> 00:35:31.150
Thank you Joseph.
This was nice.

283
00:35:36.116 --> 00:35:37.116
Are you ok?

284
00:35:38.491 --> 00:35:39.866
I'm great.

285
00:35:46.116 --> 00:35:47.191
No.

286
00:35:48.491 --> 00:35:50.741
That's Will's place.

287
00:35:51.408 --> 00:35:54.941
Big boy Will! When
is he coming here?

288
00:36:06.216 --> 00:36:08.816
Edgar. can you open the wine?

289
00:36:12.683 --> 00:36:14.916
You don't do it. I'll handle it.

290
00:36:21.158 --> 00:36:24.308
Ready-to-eat food;
I just warmed it up.

291
00:36:25.408 --> 00:36:27.321
Joseph is right; They
are very delicious.

292
00:36:27.333 --> 00:36:29.258
I wouldn't have guessed
they were frozen.

293
00:36:29.283 --> 00:36:31.483
This is worrying.

294
00:36:35.808 --> 00:36:38.250
It's pretty obvious
that they're dull food.

295
00:36:39.183 --> 00:36:41.172
If you're going to run a
restaurant. you should be

296
00:36:41.184 --> 00:36:43.303
able to tell the difference
between frozen and fresh.

297
00:36:47.733 --> 00:36:50.741
Speaking of restaurants
I don't think I will...

298
00:36:52.908 --> 00:36:57.075
- Let's talk about this another time.
- Let's talk about this now.

299
00:36:57.241 --> 00:36:58.566
We are all here.

300
00:37:00.033 --> 00:37:03.275
I haven't decided anything yet.
but it was Will's restaurant after all.

301
00:37:03.299 --> 00:37:04.499
- You two did it together.

302
00:37:06.283 --> 00:37:10.033
But you are his wife.

303
00:37:15.158 --> 00:37:16.475
Are you sure?

304
00:37:19.741 --> 00:37:23.500
Honestly for a while I had
planned to return home to Paris.

305
00:37:24.616 --> 00:37:26.691
Maybe stay with my father.

306
00:37:28.116 --> 00:37:30.275
You said you haven't
decided anything yet.

307
00:37:31.158 --> 00:37:33.333
- We have to handle this as a family.

308
00:37:34.718 --> 00:37:37.509
We have to address this as a family.

309
00:37:37.533 --> 00:37:40.075
The staff loves you.

310
00:37:41.366 --> 00:37:43.741
Alice. they need you.

311
00:37:44.325 --> 00:37:46.950
Think about Will.
Do this for him.

312
00:37:47.991 --> 00:37:49.900
Wait a minute. I know you.

313
00:37:50.866 --> 00:37:53.075
You're married to my
grandson. aren't you?

314
00:37:54.491 --> 00:37:59.033
Don't pretend to be
deaf. I asked a question.

315
00:37:59.200 --> 00:38:01.440
- I...
- No problem.

316
00:38:02.116 --> 00:38:05.783
Not only do you want to take over a
successful business. but also Will's

317
00:38:05.950 --> 00:38:10.366
I'm saying he has the
opportunity to honor his memory.

318
00:38:10.533 --> 00:38:13.616
This was his life's work. his passion.

319
00:38:13.700 --> 00:38:16.658
- You have to move this forward
- We should talk another time.

320
00:38:17.300 --> 00:38:20.717
No. it's best to put all the
cards on the table now.

321
00:38:20.741 --> 00:38:24.408
- Right.
- You're driving me crazy!

322
00:38:24.991 --> 00:38:29.325
- You are nothing without me!
- This is how Will wanted it to be.

323
00:38:29.491 --> 00:38:32.158
- This is your damn problem!
- Do this for his sake.

324
00:38:34.366 --> 00:38:36.991
We are trying to have a baby!
You don't even know what you want

325
00:38:38.491 --> 00:38:40.025
Don't drive me crazy. Alice.

326
00:38:41.700 --> 00:38:45.450
Alice. calm down.

327
00:38:47.325 --> 00:38:50.158
I'm calm.
You shouldn't speak for Will.

328
00:38:50.991 --> 00:38:55.158
I am his mother. No one
knows him better than me.

329
00:38:55.325 --> 00:38:58.308
Grandma. no...

330
00:39:01.200 --> 00:39:04.283
I am sad. We are
all here for his sake.

331
00:39:04.450 --> 00:39:05.658
Alice is right.
It's not time.

332
00:39:09.825 --> 00:39:13.033
- That's why you fail.
- Edgar. please...

333
00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:15.450
Don't you dare touch me.

334
00:39:15.616 --> 00:39:17.850
We are all mourning.
You don't have to be malicious.

335
00:39:18.075 --> 00:39:19.916
- No problem.
- No.

336
00:39:20.991 --> 00:39:21.991
Where?

337
00:39:24.491 --> 00:39:26.133
Where is the wedding ring?

338
00:39:26.825 --> 00:39:30.325
- Why don't you wear it?
- Did you sell it? At a good price?

339
00:39:30.491 --> 00:39:35.100
- No. of course not.
- Edgar. can I have the corkscrew?

340
00:39:36.866 --> 00:39:41.200
Hoodie and sneakers at
her husband's funeral...

341
00:39:41.866 --> 00:39:44.491
- I'm here. Edgar. Talk to me.
- You didn't even cry.

342
00:39:46.866 --> 00:39:50.441
- Isn't this weird?
- People grieve in different ways.

343
00:39:50.466 --> 00:39:51.466
Get lost!

344
00:40:13.158 --> 00:40:16.866
Will is dead. and now
you put us in this situation?

345
00:40:17.033 --> 00:40:20.616
- That's enough. dad.
- It's your fault he died.

346
00:40:20.783 --> 00:40:24.366
- You didn't stop him from driving!
- Stop it. dad!

347
00:40:24.533 --> 00:40:27.418
Will got into a
fight with Alice and...

348
00:40:27.430 --> 00:40:28.741
Was it my fault?

349
00:40:28.908 --> 00:40:32.533
- "Of course not."
- “You couldn't stop him either.”

350
00:40:33.783 --> 00:40:38.450
- This doesn't mean it's my fault.
- That's not what I meant.

351
00:40:38.700 --> 00:40:40.800
- Mind your own business.
You don't know anything.

352
00:40:43.033 --> 00:40:44.463
You're glad he's dead.

353
00:40:44.475 --> 00:40:47.058
Please. Will is
watching us from above.

354
00:40:49.116 --> 00:40:50.200
From above?

355
00:40:54.741 --> 00:40:55.950
He's way down.

356
00:41:17.741 --> 00:41:21.341
- Take him to the hospital!
- Thya. help me.

357
00:41:24.783 --> 00:41:26.733
What did we do to deserve this?

358
00:41:28.200 --> 00:41:30.266
They left without saying goodbye.

359
00:41:36.033 --> 00:41:38.866
- Has he completely lost his mind?
- Thya. come on...

360
00:41:40.616 --> 00:41:43.283
- He killed his dog!
- I know!

361
00:41:47.700 --> 00:41:50.325
Damn. he's bleeding everywhere.

362
00:41:55.825 --> 00:41:56.825
Joe. your father...

363
00:42:13.908 --> 00:42:14.908
NO!

364
00:42:17.533 --> 00:42:18.575
My god!

365
00:42:20.491 --> 00:42:23.241
Stop it!

366
00:42:24.950 --> 00:42:26.741
Let him go!

367
00:43:29.408 --> 00:43:31.700
"Let it go" I said!
"Shoot. for God's sake!"

368
00:43:32.741 --> 00:43:33.950
Shoot him. for God's sake!

369
00:43:34.783 --> 00:43:36.366
Shoot me.

370
00:43:36.533 --> 00:43:37.950
Shoot me. Joe.

371
00:43:38.283 --> 00:43:39.283
Shoot me.

372
00:44:02.158 --> 00:44:03.783
Joseph!

373
00:45:55.491 --> 00:45:57.241
Dating in the Cottage
Four Dead After Fire

374
00:46:00.333 --> 00:46:01.550
"October 1983."

375
00:46:02.416 --> 00:46:06.500
"That damn 'Book of the Dead.'
"I warned them not to read it."

376
00:46:06.666 --> 00:46:11.833
"Forbidden magic.
Four words that unleash evil."

377
00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:14.041
"But they didn't listen."

378
00:46:16.791 --> 00:46:20.208
"December 1983.
I finally found it."

379
00:46:20.375 --> 00:46:23.333
"A weapon that can stop them all."

380
00:46:23.500 --> 00:46:27.075
"A dagger created by
the Circle of Sages."

381
00:46:28.625 --> 00:46:30.808
"Even the slightest
wound from the ancient

382
00:46:30.820 --> 00:46:32.708
sword will sever
the demons' souls."

383
00:46:32.875 --> 00:46:35.500
"I hid it.
But I have to leave again."

384
00:46:35.666 --> 00:46:41.958
"These creatures are hunting me and
I must protect my wife and daughters."

385
00:47:03.833 --> 00:47:04.833
"Kunda."

386
00:47:15.250 --> 00:47:16.250
"Astrata."

387
00:47:28.166 --> 00:47:29.166
"Montosse."

388
00:47:40.083 --> 00:47:41.083
Fuck it.

389
00:48:19.875 --> 00:48:20.875
Alice?

390
00:48:23.833 --> 00:48:27.333
- What's the problem?
- Your dog... attacked me.

391
00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:30.500
I don't understand you.

392
00:48:34.958 --> 00:48:36.375
What happened?

393
00:48:39.625 --> 00:48:41.125
Where is your father?

394
00:48:42.166 --> 00:48:44.583
I think my father killed Thya.

395
00:48:51.750 --> 00:48:54.250
Open the door. it's me!

396
00:48:57.291 --> 00:48:59.333
He came back for my money.

397
00:50:10.875 --> 00:50:13.791
Perfect for your family.

398
00:50:16.208 --> 00:50:17.208
Cheers.

399
00:51:01.041 --> 00:51:05.625
Joe. it hurts. Please... Don't!

400
00:51:09.166 --> 00:51:10.249
Where is your father?

401
00:51:10.261 --> 00:51:12.500
We have to get out
of here. Alice. come on!

402
00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:15.000
Hurry!

403
00:51:27.458 --> 00:51:28.458
Edgar.

404
00:51:29.833 --> 00:51:32.583
- Sweetie. Let me go!
- Mom!

405
00:51:57.000 --> 00:52:01.166
You should have died. not Will.

406
00:52:06.041 --> 00:52:07.041
NO!

407
00:53:57.833 --> 00:53:59.875
NOT COVERED

408
00:54:03.208 --> 00:54:05.750
He just stands there. staring.

409
00:54:05.833 --> 00:54:09.073
- I'll be right back. mom.

410
00:54:33.125 --> 00:54:34.375
Children?

411
00:55:17.791 --> 00:55:20.083
Please open the door.

412
00:55:21.916 --> 00:55:25.208
Have you come to give
back what you stole?

413
00:55:29.666 --> 00:55:31.250
Definitely.

414
00:55:50.333 --> 00:55:53.375
My god!
Mom. are you okay?

415
00:55:54.791 --> 00:55:56.791
Mom. are you okay?

416
00:55:59.333 --> 00:56:03.000
It's okay. I have you.

417
00:56:12.708 --> 00:56:16.125
We will destroy them...

418
00:56:19.500 --> 00:56:21.625
There are no wise men anymore...

419
00:56:23.375 --> 00:56:26.750
We will destroy them...

420
00:56:30.291 --> 00:56:34.333
Should I go or do
you want to go?

421
00:56:36.833 --> 00:56:38.000
You go.

422
00:56:43.291 --> 00:56:45.291
Take my grandmother upstairs.

423
00:57:42.375 --> 00:57:46.541
Did you think that all the men
in the family would be left to you?

424
00:57:53.708 --> 00:57:55.125
Joseph. come here!

425
00:58:03.875 --> 00:58:06.291
- Help!
- Forget it. honey.

426
00:58:07.125 --> 00:58:09.333
This isn't his style.

427
00:58:11.875 --> 00:58:13.666
"Come on" I said!

428
00:58:16.375 --> 00:58:17.625
Susan...

429
00:58:18.750 --> 00:58:21.041
Stop spoiling the child.

430
00:58:23.375 --> 00:58:25.875
He has something we need.

431
00:58:56.041 --> 00:58:58.291
Give us what we came here for!

432
00:59:03.791 --> 00:59:06.291
I told you he was a thief!

433
00:59:31.625 --> 00:59:33.125
Have you become brave now?

434
00:59:56.541 --> 00:59:57.708
Boo!

435
01:00:22.000 --> 01:00:27.041
I was your first... And I'll
make sure I'm your last.

436
01:00:49.208 --> 01:00:51.833
So you refused to shoot your father.

437
01:00:54.333 --> 01:00:55.958
But killing me...

438
01:01:10.875 --> 01:01:12.375
Is it easy?

439
01:01:17.083 --> 01:01:19.916
Come here young lady! I
have what you are looking for!

440
01:01:28.083 --> 01:01:29.916
I'll be right back. honey.

441
01:01:50.250 --> 01:01:55.833
The money is under the bed.
Take this and leave us alone.

442
01:01:59.166 --> 01:02:01.666
This place is a complete mess.

443
01:02:03.333 --> 01:02:08.166
But there's something we
want inside your little head.

444
01:02:10.791 --> 01:02:13.625
Your husband must
have told you where he is.

445
01:02:44.291 --> 01:02:46.291
This will fix you.

446
01:02:54.833 --> 01:02:55.958
Polly...

447
01:02:57.208 --> 01:02:58.708
Where's your leg?

448
01:03:09.583 --> 01:03:10.833
That little...

449
01:03:16.250 --> 01:03:18.792
The Circle of Wise
Failed. Your grandfather

450
01:03:18.804 --> 01:03:21.125
is a failure. You
will all die tonight.

451
01:04:14.750 --> 01:04:16.583
Alice...

452
01:04:18.541 --> 01:04:20.250
I'm coming. Alice.

453
01:04:22.291 --> 01:04:24.625
Your time is up.

454
01:04:58.458 --> 01:05:02.250
Joe. what is the "Circle of Wise"?

455
01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:07.000
- I didn't think they were real.
- Tell me.

456
01:05:07.166 --> 01:05:09.416
I saw distorted drawings.

457
01:05:12.041 --> 01:05:14.541
Did Will say anything
about our grandfather?

458
01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:22.916
As children. we were always
told that he was unstable.

459
01:05:23.083 --> 01:05:28.708
In his diaries. he described a group
who believed that the devil was there.

460
01:05:28.875 --> 01:05:32.875
And if anyone reads the
thing they'll come back...

461
01:05:35.833 --> 01:05:37.458
"The Book of the Dead".

462
01:05:45.916 --> 01:05:49.208
My grandfather left the
family and traveled the world to

463
01:05:49.375 --> 01:05:53.666
research and collect objects
that would protect us from this.

464
01:05:53.833 --> 01:05:55.250
Are they still there?

465
01:05:56.916 --> 01:06:00.083
My mother wanted me to throw
everything away when she died. but...

466
01:06:00.250 --> 01:06:02.916
- But what happened AQ...
- But I didn't.

467
01:06:03.625 --> 01:06:07.791
There are still a few things
in the attic. And Thya...

468
01:06:08.750 --> 01:06:12.291
The creature inside said they
were looking for something.

469
01:06:13.083 --> 01:06:15.666
Maybe this will stop them.

470
01:06:21.875 --> 01:06:24.083
Mom. drink this.

471
01:06:30.250 --> 01:06:32.333
Can you look under the bed?

472
01:06:32.500 --> 01:06:36.333
Your father always made sure
there were no monsters there.

473
01:06:47.250 --> 01:06:50.500
- There are no monsters.
- You are lying.

474
01:06:54.041 --> 01:06:57.291
Don't worry. you're safe here.

475
01:07:08.708 --> 01:07:09.958
Good night mom.

476
01:07:14.750 --> 01:07:16.375
Good night. Susan.

477
01:07:20.083 --> 01:07:21.750
What did you say to me?

478
01:07:55.833 --> 01:07:57.458
Come on honey.

479
01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:12.000
Mom...

480
01:08:13.625 --> 01:08:15.625
I miss you.

481
01:08:17.208 --> 01:08:20.833
I miss you a lot.

482
01:08:23.333 --> 01:08:27.750
We share the same
dream. It can still happen.

483
01:08:28.875 --> 01:08:32.250
The whole family can be reunited.

484
01:08:34.625 --> 01:08:39.125
Will is already on his
way. It will be here soon.

485
01:08:48.208 --> 01:08:50.208
Don't be afraid. Susan.

486
01:09:01.500 --> 01:09:04.333
Remember what you said at the funeral.

487
01:09:05.416 --> 01:09:08.208
That you can give everything...

488
01:09:08.375 --> 01:09:11.791
so we can all be together again.

489
01:09:39.916 --> 01:09:42.666
You are nothing without your family.

490
01:09:52.083 --> 01:09:54.083
I miss you.

491
01:09:56.041 --> 01:09:57.875
I miss us.

492
01:11:25.208 --> 01:11:28.625
You haven't kissed
me like this in years.

493
01:11:44.708 --> 01:11:46.916
Your father is gone;
maybe we can...

494
01:11:50.958 --> 01:11:51.958
Joseph?

495
01:11:54.333 --> 01:11:57.131
Is my grandmother
okay? Is everything ok?

496
01:11:57.143 --> 01:11:59.250
Yes. everything is better now.

497
01:12:01.500 --> 01:12:03.250
You must trust me.

498
01:12:04.916 --> 01:12:08.250
- "Trust you?"
- "They are not our enemies."

499
01:12:08.416 --> 01:12:12.875
I understand this now. They just want
something back that my father stole.

500
01:12:13.041 --> 01:12:16.291
I told you he was a bad man.

501
01:12:16.458 --> 01:12:19.375
It's very simple. Just
tell them where you are.

502
01:12:19.541 --> 01:12:22.708
Give them what they want.
